.TH FTREE 1
.SH NAME
ftree \- namespace browser and file tree viewer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/ftree
[
.B \-n
] [
.I root
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ftree
is a Draw-based file tree viewer and interactive namespace browser
for Inferno that runs under the
.IR wm (1)
window manager or any window manager providing a
.IR draw (3)
context.
It displays the filesystem as an expandable tree with keyboard
and mouse navigation, a scrollbar, and a context menu.
.PP
Unlike Tk-based tree viewers,
.I ftree
uses the native widget toolkit (see
.IR widget (2))
and runs in the Lucifer presentation view alongside
.IR edit (1),
.IR sh (1),
and
.IR man (1).
.PP
If a
.I root
argument is given,
.I ftree
starts browsing from that directory instead of
.BR / .
.SS Namespace Mode
With the
.B \-n
flag or by pressing
.BR Ctrl-N ,
.I ftree
enters namespace mode, which annotates tree nodes with live
metadata from the process's mount table
.RB ( /prog/\fIpid\fP/ns ).
.PP
In namespace mode, each directory that has a bind or mount
entry shows its source path and flags inline.
For example:
.PP
.EX
  v dev/       -b #c [+2]
  v net/       #I
    > ssl/     #D
.EE
.PP
This means
.B /dev
is bound from kernel device
.B #c
with the
.B -b
(before) flag and has 2 additional union layers;
.B /net
is a mount of
.BR #I ;
.B /dev/ssl
is device
.BR #D .
.PP
Union directories \(em created by
.B "bind -b"
or
.B "bind -a"
\(em display a layer count in brackets.
Kernel device paths
.RB ( #c ,
.BR #d ,
.BR #I ,
etc.) are coloured distinctly from regular mounts.
.PP
A background watcher polls the namespace every 2 seconds
and auto-refreshes the display when external bind, mount,
or unmount operations change the mount table.
.SS Namespace Operations
.I Ftree
supports interactive namespace manipulation:
.TP
.B "Bind (Ctrl-B)"
Prompts for a source path, then for flags
.RB ( -b
for before,
.B -a
for after,
.B -c
for create; or empty for replace).
Calls
.IR sys-bind (2)
directly on the selected directory.
The tree and namespace annotations refresh automatically.
.TP
.B "Unmount (Ctrl-U)"
Unmounts the top binding on the selected directory using
.IR sys-bind (2).
Only available when the selected directory has a bind source
in the mount table.
.PP
These operations modify the current process's namespace and
take effect immediately.
.SS Plumbing
When a file is activated (Enter key, Button 2, or context menu),
.I ftree
sends a plumb message via
.IR plumbmsg (2)
with attributes derived from the file type:
.PP
.TP
.B ".b .m .sh"
\fIkind\fP=text, action=showfile (opens in editor)
.TP
.B ".dis"
\fIkind\fP=text, action=showdata
.TP
.B ".bit .jpg .png .gif"
\fIkind\fP=image
.TP
.B ".html .htm"
\fIkind\fP=text, action=showurl
.TP
.I "other"
\fIkind\fP=text, action=showfile
.PP
If no plumber is running, the status bar reports an error.
.SS Keyboard
.TP
.B Up / Down
Move selection up or down.
.TP
.B Left
Collapse directory, or move selection to parent.
.TP
.B "Right / Enter"
Expand directory, or plumb file.
.TP
.B "Page Up / Page Down"
Scroll by screenful.
.TP
.B "Home / End"
Jump to first or last item.
.TP
.B Ctrl-B
Start bind operation (prompted in status bar).
.TP
.B Ctrl-G
Goto path (prompted in status bar).
.TP
.B Ctrl-N
Toggle namespace annotations on or off.
.TP
.B Ctrl-U
Unmount selected directory.
.TP
.B Ctrl-Q
Quit.
.TP
.B "r / R"
Refresh tree (re-read directories).
.SS Mouse
.TP
.B Button 1
Select item.
Clicking the expand/collapse triangle toggles the directory.
.TP
.B Button 2
Plumb selected file.
.TP
.B Button 3
Context menu.
The menu adapts to the selection:
directories show expand/collapse and namespace operations;
files show plumb; mounted directories show unmount.
.TP
.B Scroll wheel
Scroll up or down.
.SS Display
Directories are drawn in bold with a trailing
.BR / .
File sizes are shown right-aligned in a dim colour.
In namespace mode, bind sources and flags replace file sizes
for mounted directories.
.PP
Directories sort before files within each level.
The tree supports lazy loading: directory contents are read
on first expansion.
.PP
.I Ftree
supports theming via
.IR lucitheme (2).
Kernel device paths are shown in the theme's green colour;
mount annotations in yellow; selection highlight uses the
accent colour.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /dis/wm/ftree.dis
Compiled file tree viewer.
.TP
.B /tmp/veltro/ftree/state
Current state for Veltro agents (root, selection, item count).
.TP
.B /tmp/veltro/ftree/view
Plain text rendering of visible tree for AI context.
.TP
.B /tmp/veltro/ftree/ctl
Command interface for Veltro agents.
.SS Veltro Control Commands
Write to
.B /tmp/veltro/ftree/ctl
to control the tree viewer:
.TP
.BI "cd " path
Change root to
.IR path .
.TP
.BI "goto " path
Same as
.BR cd .
.TP
.BI "select " path
Select the node at
.IR path .
.TP
.B expand
Expand selected directory.
.TP
.B collapse
Collapse selected directory.
.TP
.B refresh
Refresh tree from filesystem.
.TP
.B nsmode
Toggle namespace annotations.
.TP
.BI "bind " "src target" " [flags]"
Bind
.I src
onto
.I target
with optional
.IR flags .
.TP
.BI "unmount " path
Unmount
.IR path .
.TP
.BI "scroll " direction
Scroll:
.BR up ,
.BR down ,
.BR top ,
.BR bottom .
